A||||2||JohnnyK||What else should I do with the motor out?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||10-12-2000||07:37 PM||||I'm planning on selling the car after the winter, and I want to know what I should do while the engine is out. I am adding clearance to the clutch shafts, so I'm going to put a new clutch in, and I was thinking timing chain (It's a duke with 138000 miles on it).. Anything else? I have to do little minor things like put a heat shield over the starter, but major things? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||10-12-2000||07:57 PM||||The Duke uses a gear drive, not a chain.  I have never had to do this repair yet, so I can't help.  I would suggest doing this while the engine is out, but if you are selling it I wouldn't bother (assuming it runs just fine and doesn't need it done).<P>I'd snug up all of the bolts and whatnot.....maybe replace the exhaust manifold gasket (check manifold for cracks too), valve cover gasket and pan gasket.  The pan gasket is a bugger to get at with it in the car, so now would be a good time if it is leaking.<P><BR>If you plan on selling it then I wouldn't go too crazy with it, but if you can seal up a few oil leaks it will make it easier to sell.<P><BR>Good luck.    ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-12-2000||08:41 PM||||RodrV6 has done the cam gears a couple times.. he could point you in a direction.. <P>rodrv6@yahoo.com<P>Rod Schneider (great guy!)||||reg||1
